dp_filedate":1792583865000,"nhcTitle":"Offshore of the East Coast of the United States (AL93)","discussion":"A storm-force non-tropical low pressure area located a few hundred  miles off the mid-Atlantic United States coast is producing some  shower and thunderstorm activity primarily west and northwest of its  center. Over the next day or two, the low could gradually lose its  frontal features while it moves slowly north-northeastward over the  Gulf Stream, allowing the system to possibly develop subtropical  characteristics. By Friday, the system is expected to accelerate  northeastward away from the the eastern United States, and  environmental conditions are expected to become unfavorable for  additional subtropical or tropical development.  1. Regardless of the status of the system, high winds, coastal  flooding, and dangerous surf are expected along portions of the U.S.  East Coast during the next few days. For more information, please  consult statements and warnings from local National Weather Service  offices and the Weather Prediction Center, along with the High Seas  Forecasts and the Storm Warnings issued by the National Weather  Service. \n Formation chance through 48 hours...medium...40 percent. \n Formation chance through 7 days...medium...40 percent.","disturbance":1}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-99.45022465886238,8.40706309406852],[-99.40070951102621,8.399031354455515],[-99.35171999900409,8.391623787958823],[-99.30323690772786,8.384849423487216],[-99.25524102212938,8.378717289949474],[-99.20771312714044,8.373236416254375],[-99.16063400769292,8.368415831310697],[-99.11398444871864,8.364264564027213],[-99.0677452351494,8.360791643312702],[-99.02189715191709,8.358006098075943],[-98.97642098395352,8.355916957225709],[-98.93129751619053,8.354533249670782],[-98.88650753355994,8.353864004319936],[-98.8420318209936,8.353918250081952],[-98.79785116342336,8.354705015865601],[-98.753946345781,8.356233330579665],[-98.7102981